Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.780
I know it is a difficult task, but you can do it.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.020
Episode 3:
I'm Sorry

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.400
No, I want you to do your best to accomplish it.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.200
All right, that's it for today.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.210
The mid-term exams for the first semester are next week.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.300
Study very hard and be ready for them!

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:23.650
This isn't good.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:25.460
I don't understand it at all...

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.460
I know.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:27.470
Arrrgh!

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:29.320
I don't want it, don't want it, don't want it!

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.610
I don't want to attend the supplementary classes!

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.590
I know.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:33.980
Damn boy scout Jinrai!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.980
How the heck are we supposed to solve this?

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:37.970
I know.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.690
Huh?

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:40.310
I know.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:41.960
I know.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.130
Now, the tongue twister!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.590
"She sells sea shells by the sea shore."

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.570
I know.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:52.370
Arisa is a very cute girl.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.410
I know.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:55.720
Shipon's gonna buy me today's lunch!

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.620
No thanks.

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.260
This is the program he was talking about in class.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.480
And...

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:06.250
Whoa!

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.540
I added a little bit extra to his program...

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:13.100
...and I turned it into this more realistic simulation model.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:15.380
No good?

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:16.370
I guess...

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:17.840
Shipon.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:18.270
What?

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:20.040
Teach me that!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.530
Please teach us!

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.220
What!?

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:27.990
Hi!

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.950
So, how is the general meeting going so far?

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.990
It seems like they are trying a little too hard.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.590
It's more like they're so full of themselves.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:41.160
I wish they were more serious since the entire human race...

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.750
...will face the danger of extinction if the Great Mission fails.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.040
You want them to start fighting or something?

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.600
No, what I meant was...

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:53.610
Well, we've known what we're supposed to do since 189 years ago.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.910
So this is more like a...

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.780
...the Pre-Great Mission Party.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.680
Yeah, I think it's something like that.

00:04:02.030 --> 00:04:02.840
Hmm...

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.670
Now, Foundation 6...

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.530
...Mr. Sergei Roskov, please proceed.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.520
Well, then, please take a look at the monitor.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:20.530
The star Hydrus Beta's supernova...

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:23.430
Well, so-called hydrous blast, that is.

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:28.110
The First Wave only contained a pure electromagnetic energy...

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.670
...but the Second Wave has mass.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.650
The Wave's speed is one tenth of the First Wave...

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.090
...but the destruction it brings could be greater than that of the First.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:42.420
The current location is seven light days from the Sun...

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.100
Seven light days...

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.530
That's 70 days, which means...

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.010
Right before Christmas.

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:54.570
The Second Wave is coming in straight against the ecliptic.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:57.110
So all the Foundations other than number 6...

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.010
...will begin the mission almost at the same time.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:00.870
Look!

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:02.640
Headmaster! Headmaster!

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:04.610
He doesn't look good on camera.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.630
He looks like a criminal.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:12.560
Foundation 4 El Santo Commander, Mr. Kurt Wagner.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.760
You said that Foundation 6 is only 80% ready right now...

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.210
...so I'd like to ask you this.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:25.100
In fact, can you actually test the Great Wall prior to the actual event?

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:26.810
Yes.

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.030
Foundation 6 Ultima...

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.300
...will have contact with the Second Wave 42 days from now.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:39.790
But the barrier will be ready to be activated 14 days prior to that.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.730
Ultima will be absolutely ready.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:47.600
Bravo!

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:01.800
Huh?

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:09.640
All right!

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:29.040
And... And... And... And...

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.230
Arrrgh!

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.230
How am I supposed to clean this place!?

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:34.650
Ugh...

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:40.170
Actually, why do I have to clean the house by myself?

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:42.830
Arisa went out shopping by herself...

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:46.970
Arisa?

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:52.750
After all, Arisa is the one who came up with this study group idea!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:53.730
Geez...

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:55.610
Arisa...!

00:06:58.820 --> 00:06:59.600
Oh...

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.770
Arisa-sa...

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:07.990
Hello.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:11.040
The study group is here, right?

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:11.950
Y-Yes.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.310
Um... Well...

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:19.320
This is, um...

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.950
I'm Kouta Otoyama.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.250
Oh, I'm Shima Katase.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.100
"Arisa-sa." What song is that?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:27.740
What?

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.680
Oh, no, well...

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.760
I was... Um...

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:32.250
Hm?

00:07:33.900 --> 00:07:34.930
I'm home!

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.530
Oh, hello.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:37.800
Hello!

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.630
Huh!? Kouta.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:40.230
Hey!

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:41.600
Who's that?

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.040
He's always by himself, so I invited him.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:46.100
I see.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.130
Shipon, a present!

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:49.570
No need to thank us.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:50.210
Huh...

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:54.230
And flowers for the lady.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.570
Well then, thank you so much.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.540
Shipon, a vase!

00:07:58.910 --> 00:07:59.610
Oh, yes!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:01.960
Arrrrgh!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:04.120
I still don't get it!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:11.600
I mean, why do we have to design such a difficult program?

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.020
This is the simulation of the Great Wall, right?

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.540
It's not like we're going to use it, you know.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:21.750
But the future of our solar system is depending on this mission...

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.010
...so we have to understand the basics.

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:28.210
Some seniors in the main course will probably join this mission, right?

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.280
It's so exciting!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.500
If I had been born a few years earlier...!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:36.040
I think you'd still be studying with us like this...

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.010
...because you might have failed to make grades.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:38.820
Hey!

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:45.840
You made a very impressive remark earlier, but this is not impressive.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.120
Yeah, I'm not good at this kind of thing.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:51.950
Looks like it.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:53.620
Shipon.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:54.110
Huh?

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:56.720
Go ahead and teach him.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:08:57.930
What?

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.350
It would be great!

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:02.410
Thanks, Ms. Katase!

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:05.020
S-Sure...

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:23.780
Wow!

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.970
The most important thing in this simulation is to balance...

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:30.140
...both the electromagnetic barrier and the anti-gravity force.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.010
Hmm?

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.050
Yes, yes, I got that.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:33.640
By the way...

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.540
...how come the barrier has two layers?

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:38.150
Oh, that...

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.520
The electromagnetic barrier will bounce back...

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.090
...the electrons and magnetic particles.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:51.470
And anti-gravity force will bounce back much larger particles.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.390
The actual barrier contains a number of individual barriers.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.080
Now here is the question!

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.680
How many layers are actually in the barrier?

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:01.460
W-Well...

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:02.970
120 layers!

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:03.720
You are right!

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:04.700
Impressive!

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:06.690
All right then.

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.880
My prize is a date with you.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.990
Hey, this is Usako's stuffed animal, right?

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.360
It's so big!

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:15.730
Can I see it?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:16.930
Um, oh, no!

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:22.830
Shipon?

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:26.000
Well, I couldn't clean the house that quick!

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:34.980
Arisa's Stuff 

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:30.350
Don't stuff everything in the closet!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.740
Clean it up for Christ sake!

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:33.880
Hey, a pair of shorts...

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:34.810
I-Idiot!

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.260
How come there is no soundproofing here?

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.240
After all, this is the Universe Academy's dorm...

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.880
Oh, that.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.480
I've heard that their intention is to give us some inconvenience...

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.240
...so we have to help each other out...

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:55.540
...and learn how to care for each other under the same roof.

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:00.410
The first step of life outside space begins in our private life!

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.100
Then I'm even more convinced.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:02.940
What?

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:04.360
I'm going to shut them up!

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.160
Take care...

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:11.610
Huh?

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.230
All right!

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.550
Now...let's go!!

00:11:27.630 --> 00:11:28.890
Yeah!

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:34.170
And, if you repeat this sub-routine...

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:37.150
...this number becomes smaller and smaller, right?

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:38.560
Wow...

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:40.340
That's incredible.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:42.180
I didn't know that.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.570
I can explain it to you in much more detail.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:49.850
What are you doing?

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:53.690
Oh, I'm accessing the main server of the Stellvia.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:57.030
If you do this, you can use the actual live data...

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.660
...so the simulation will be more realistic!

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.460
This time all at the same time!

00:12:02.710 --> 00:12:03.430
At the same time!

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:04.420
At the same time!

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.280
He did it together!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:07.780
See!

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:10.470
If you sandwich the anti-gravity barrier...

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.400
...between the electromagnetic barriers...

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.970
...you can add as many layers as you want.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:17.240
Wow, it's so cool!

00:12:17.950 --> 00:12:21.380
But, is it Okay to pull this data out of the main server?

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:22.630
No problem!

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.530
Because we're not overwriting or anything.

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:29.550
Besides, I'm accessing it as our headmaster.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.200
S-Seriously?

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.040
Look at that!

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.340
Hey, is it Dai-chan?

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.960
What are you two doing?

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.560
Yeah, take a look at this!

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:40.670
This is so cool!

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:41.430
Hmm?

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.250
They don't lock the door?

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:58.690
How careless...

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.720
Usako...

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.230
My Sweet...

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.670
You guys are too loud!

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:08.670
Usako...

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.930
Usako...

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.030
I said you guys are too loud!!

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:19.580
Ms. Akira Kayama is in the house!!

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.110
Hey!

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.250
Yay!

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:24.650
It's Akira!

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:27.550
Geez, you scared me.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:30.010
Hm?

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:36.290
Shipon?

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:37.640
What's the matter?

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:41.000
Stellvia's program...

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.560
...was overwritten...

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.720
What!?

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.500
Undo what you just did!!

00:13:46.570 --> 00:13:47.330
Okay...

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:51.200
Well...

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:52.250
Bye.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:53.610
Don't leave now!

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:56.810
But even if I was able to put everything back...

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:59.220
...I can't delete the access log.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:01.720
Oh, because you actually changed the data...

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:05.690
...the machine will record the log of that activity.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:07.690
This is not a joke at all!

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.820
Do something!

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.300
Come on, come on, come on!

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.990
If we go to the machine room...

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:15.870
...and access the server directly,  maybe we can do something about it.

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:16.480
That's it!

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:27.290
Yes?

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:29.370
It's me, Fujisawa.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.280
What can I do for you?

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:37.910
Ms. Machida.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:42.010
Since you are the residence manager, I want to ask you about something.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:46.610
Hmm? Is there anything wrong?

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:49.150
We're coming in!

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:54.840
Maybe they went out with Ms. Kayama.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:56.710
That's impossible!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.710
She's very serious and she was quite angry at them, so...

00:15:01.010 --> 00:15:02.020
Hmm...

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.940
Warned them and they got upset, and they ganged up on her...

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.370
What!?

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.710
That's not good!

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:09.710
We must stop them!

00:15:10.410 --> 00:15:12.850
W-Wait, just wait a minute!

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:20.970
Wow...

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:25.390
Dai-chan, the machine room is the other way.

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.140
There is no point rushing.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.770
So, just leave it to me.

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.110
But who caused all this?

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.400
Because of you all.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:37.210
Actually, it's because of your shouting!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.080
Hey, hey.

00:15:38.340 --> 00:15:41.060
We've got to do something about it, or we'll be expelled.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.320
W-What!?

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.620
You idiot! Don't scare us like that!

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.860
We'll be okay, Shipon.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:53.870
Wow!

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:54.560
Hmph!

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.280
Hmm...

00:16:03.150 --> 00:16:05.040
Are you all students?

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:07.410
Oh, we are freshmen.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.140
What are freshmen like you doing at a place like this?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:11.450
Um, well...

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:15.680
It's actually a small thing, but it's extremely serious and...

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:16.480
Hmm!?

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:19.520
Hey, you guys.

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:21.570
Yo!

00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:25.070
Big 4, Kent Austin.

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:25.900
Yes.

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:27.760
They are my friends.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.150
Friends?

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:29.770
Yes.

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:33.460
They came here to pick me up.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.370
Thank you so so much!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:38.740
You are very welcome.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.590
From now on, you should plan well if you want to play around here.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:43.630
See ya!

00:16:44.070 --> 00:16:45.380
Banzai!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:46.780
Sorry for your trouble.

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:49.080
This is mortifying, but I must admit...

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:52.250
...I finally met my rival for the first time in my life.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:53.320
Yeah, right.

00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:55.900
Hey! Over here!

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.120
Now where are we going?

00:16:58.150 --> 00:16:59.990
Let's see, this time...

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:01.420
What!?

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:09.950
This is the giant air duct going vertically...

00:17:10.010 --> 00:17:11.390
...all the way through the Stellvia.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:15.620
If we climb this up, we'll come out right underneath the machine room!

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:16.350
Are you sure?

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:18.720
Are we really climbing this up?

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:20.500
If we don't, we're expelled.

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:23.570
Let's do our best, Shipon!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:27.670
I saw them.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.330
You mean Kent's friends?

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.860
Yeah, I saw them.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:33.990
All of them?

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:36.870
They were just wandering around in one group.

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:40.080
Where did you see them last?

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:44.310
I looked down...

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:45.540
I'm scared...

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.420
You can do it, Shipon!

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:50.980
Watch out, duck!

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.290
It's okay now.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:00.350
Huh--Oh!

00:18:01.830 --> 00:18:02.760
Follow me.

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:05.230
Damn!

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.530
This is incredible!

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:09.110
This is a trash shoot.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.200
You should choose some other route.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:12.670
I see...

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:14.340
Oh, that's true.

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.540
This is a trash shoot.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:19.060
And, um...

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.370
What are you doing in here?

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:23.460
Training.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:24.000
What?

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:25.480
So long!

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.280
Damn, so cool...

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:30.650
I believe he is one of the Big 4.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.130
His name is...

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:33.230
Like a ninja...

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.360
What are they up to climbing up the place like this?

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:39.300
I have no idea.

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.100
What's going on in here today?

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.200
Soujin?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.270
Training again?

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.810
Oh, Ayaka.

00:18:51.390 --> 00:18:53.210
Have you seen a group of strange kids?

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.790
This is our academy's hangar!

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:03.500
After all that? Are you kidding me?

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.360
Don't complain.

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:08.220
We have to change our route anyway.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:11.360
Is that new route much harder than the last one?

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.450
Something bad may happen...

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:17.570
We are outside now!

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.650
If we can't make it inside, then try outside!

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:24.180
You're not thinking of anything at all, are you?

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.670
If we keep going, we'll come to the hatch behind the machine room.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:29.100
Are you sure about that?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:30.770
Huh?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:35.890
What is it?

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:37.190
Um...

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:39.480
What are you doing here?

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.600
I'm enjoying the Earth.

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:46.420
I see...

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:49.970
The Earth...

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.950
We came all the way...

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.340
We can't waste our time like this!

00:19:57.410 --> 00:19:58.530
Hurry, hurry!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.760
Excuse us!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.910
Hey, wait for me!

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:09.870
Oh, this star-filled sky, this land...

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:12.440
What else is out there...?

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.790
But what about the security system guarding the whole Stellvia?

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.820
I turned it off.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:25.400
What!?

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.260
Done!

00:20:26.960 --> 00:20:28.070
Right on!

00:20:28.720 --> 00:20:30.910
Shipon can be a great thief!

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.040
You think so?

00:20:38.030 --> 00:20:38.990
Hurry up, Shipon.

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:39.480
Okay.

00:20:42.990 --> 00:20:44.390
Y-You guys!

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.320
You guys...

00:20:47.690 --> 00:20:49.650
S-Sabotage!?

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:51.510
Is it!?

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:52.000
Eek!

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.130
Answer me!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.040
Something bad...

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:03.620
...may happen.

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:05.970
No, actually, it's already happening.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.800
Arrgh... I'll be expelled...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:10.360
I'll be arrested...!

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:22.020
Hey! We've just started!

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:22.990
Shut up and sit still!

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:28.000
I won't let any dangerous animals like you get expelled so easily!

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.030
Is there anything wrong?

00:21:31.730 --> 00:21:35.130
It's about the program that a student named Katase created...

00:21:35.490 --> 00:21:35.950
Mmm...

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:37.140
Well...

00:21:37.510 --> 00:21:39.770
They said she created it in just one night.

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:40.980
This?

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:44.840
And there's no bug whatsoever...

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:49.720
I-I'm sorry...

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:52.960
I'm sorry!!

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.360 --> 00:22:00.890
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:07.570
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.330
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:21.240
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:29.020
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:35.940
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:42.730
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.860 --> 00:22:51.900
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.510 --> 00:22:58.950
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
And still I looked up

00:22:59.170 --> 00:23:04.860
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.070
Next Episode

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:06.970
Hello! It's me, Arisa!

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:11.400
We're finally getting used to life at he academy and we're all doing well.

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:13.340
But Shipon is not so well.

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:14.200
She is exhausted.

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:17.240
Because of the flying training of the Ora-avis Machine!

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:19.390
This training is extremely difficult...

00:23:19.530 --> 00:23:21.380
...but Shipon is already marked by Ms. Leila...

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:23.840
...who yells at her "This and that, this and that, this and that, this and that."

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:25.920
Because she's doing so well in other classes...

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.790
...her clumsiness in this class stands out so much!

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:29.050
Hold out, Shipon!

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:30.560
I'm with you all the way!

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.500
Next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "I'll do my best!"

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.100
      Episode 4:
I'll Do My Best!

00:23:33.880 --> 00:23:34.750
Please watch it!
